f-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Kickoff: created /Users/joeoakhart/fix-3b93-review-bot-test-lifespan from current origin/main 0ed21609f4; provisioned the pinned Python 3.12 worktree venv and verified hooks. Preflight confirmed this is a ready leaf. Updated the plan and declared tests/conftest.py plus tests/unit/test_review_bot.py as the complete edit set. Landing path is one Gerrit change to refs/for/main, gated by LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, then plain Submit, mirror confirmation, and ticket close.","timestamp":1786142783392574001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review response: adopted the concrete-baseline advisory by pinning the suite value to 1.0s. Re-ran the string-reference census and classified all five sites: three identical setup sites are de-duplicated; the janitor-wiring test retains only its observable janitor fake; the shutdown-cancel test retains only its slow-reconciler fault injection. Re-reviewing because this material plan improvement correctly staled the first attestation.","timestamp":1786143175231021001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Claimed successfully as joeoakhart@navapbc.com after a fresh certified plan-review attestation at origin/main 0ed21609f4. Beginning RED-first work now. Test contract: TestClient enters the real app lifespan; default test harness must bound shutdown to 1.0s and replace reconciler/janitor background work, while a marked control proves the real reconcile_loop remains opt-in and deterministic.","timestamp":1786143417736827001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RED evidence: tests/unit/test_review_bot.py::test_lifespan_is_safe_by_default_without_per_test_stubs entered TestClient(app), returned /health 200 with the exact payload, and tore down in under 2s; it then failed at the intended contract because shutdown_drain_seconds() was 1200.0, not the test-only 1.0 baseline. Focused command exited 1 in 0.90s. This proves the pre-fix harness lacks the global bound while the regression traverses the real lifespan.","timestamp":1786143499905675001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"GREEN and review evidence: focused lifespan contracts 8/8 passed; full tests/unit/test_review_bot.py 86/86 passed; defect-seeded mutation restoring a 1200s test value re-failed the RED oracle exactly; make check passed Ruff/format/complexity/policy/workflow lint/mypy; authoritative macOS CI selection with required extras, xdist -n3/worksteal, and the 300s thread timeout passed 11,382 tests with 19 expected skips in 13m16s. Five-axis self-review found no blocking issue; strengthened controls now assert the production constant is exactly 1200 and the local drain test reads exactly 0.1. Production files remain untouched.","timestamp":1786144842120022001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Committed 85ea9cb1f0 (Change-Id I31ddec2708f149bac785b6536833cb07c97e9e5f) with DCO sign-off and a resolving rebar-ticket trailer. The enabled local review-code preview completed against the attested commit with PASS: 0 blocking, 0 advisory; tests and deletion-impact overlays also found no issues. Pushing this exact commit for Gerrit review.","timestamp":1786145114766423001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit patchset 1 exposed one CI-only policy failure: scripts/check_wall_clock_asserts.py required an inline rationale on the intentional <2s hang guard. Added the sanctioned timing: hang-guard comment (non-behavioral), then passed the exact wall-clock guard, make check, and the focused lifespan regression. Amended the same Change-Id as commit 633a1798be and pushed patchset 2 to change 1526.","timestamp":1786145420443500001}],"created_at":1786142124703335001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"302208df-a73e-4bfc-a927-1da06f1592af","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"89d5-61da-b621-47f8"},{"link_uuid":"8a3b24ae-b989-41d6-ad4a-41e369429787","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"db8b-0b2a-f592-4d82"},{"link_uuid":"ae4470a2-7903-444a-88f2-0b6598cd3312","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2ae0-abdf-99df-4e69"},{"link_uuid":"1a713258-f241-4e93-8676-7557824ec7f2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"601f-3a7b-3705-4d31"},{"link_uuid":"5cf94f7a-7ef4-4211-af67-ef313d99947c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"478a-15bb-204f-4485"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nEntering the review-bot ASGI lifespan from an ordinary test starts the real backfill reconciler and snapshot janitor, while shutdown reads the production 1200-second queue-drain default. The idiomatic `with TestClient(app)` path can therefore turn a unit test into a long-running background sweep/hang. The production default is intentional and must not change: `src/rebar/review_bot/config.py:49` defines `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS = 1200`, and `shutdown_drain_seconds()` at `src/rebar/review_bot/config.py:92` already accepts a positive `SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS` override.\n\n## Approach\nUse the existing environment knob in the root pytest harness to pin `SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS=1.0` for every test. In `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py`, add one module autouse fixture that stubs `reconcile.reconcile_loop` and `rebar._snapshot.start_background_janitor` by default. A registered `real_reconcile_loop` marker will explicitly bypass only the reconciler stub for tests that exercise the real loop; the janitor remains stubbed because its filesystem sweep is unrelated to those contracts.\n\nThe full string-reference inventory is deliberate: remove the identical idle-reconciler plus no-op-janitor setup at current lines 1446-1449, 1474-1477, and 1615-1618. At lines 1232-1237, retain the test-specific `fake_start` janitor override because that test observes start/stop signaling, but use the new default idle reconciler instead of its duplicate. At lines 1723-1725, retain the test-specific `_slow_reconcile_loop` override because it is the shutdown-cancel fault injection, while removing its redundant no-op janitor patch. This centralizes safe defaults without shadowing tests whose contract requires a specialized fake.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/conftest.py`: register the opt-out marker and set the exact suite-wide `SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS=1.0` baseline that individual tests may override.\n- `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py`: add the module autouse stubs and RED-first lifespan/escape-hatch coverage; remove redundant per-test stubs while retaining the classified purpose-specific overrides.\n- No production files change; `src/rebar/review_bot/config.py` remains the authoritative production default and parser.\n\n## Testing\n- RED oracle: enter the real app lifespan through `TestClient` without any per-test background-task stubs and require a prompt successful health response; before the module fixture exists, the focused test is bounded by pytest-timeout and fails instead of inheriting a long shutdown.\n- Default path: the new autouse fixture makes the lifespan test prompt while the suite-wide environment value is exactly `1.0`.\n- Escape hatch: a `real_reconcile_loop`-marked lifespan test replaces only `reconcile_once` with a deterministic observable fake and proves the production `reconcile_loop` actually runs.\n- Override/control: the existing drain-specific test sets `SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS=0.1` and remains green; the stop-grace test continues to compute its floor from `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS`, pinning the production 1200-second constant.\n- Gates: focused pytest nodes first, then `make check` and `make test` using the worktree virtualenv; CI additionally exercises the required optional-extra lane.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every pytest test receives the exact `SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS=1.0` baseline; verified by a root-conftest contract test and the focused review-bot tests.\n- [ ] The production default remains 1200 seconds; verified by the unchanged `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS` and the existing stop-grace-period test.\n- [ ] A test-local `SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS=0.1` override wins over the suite baseline; verified by `test_lifespan_drain_is_bounded` remaining green.\n- [ ] Entering the review-bot lifespan is safe by default with no per-test reconciler/janitor stubs; verified by a new prompt TestClient health-path regression test.\n- [ ] All five existing string-referenced stub sites are classified: three identical setup sites are removed, the janitor-wiring test retains only its observable janitor fake, and the slow-cancel test retains only its fault-injection reconciler; verified by focused tests and the final grep/diff.\n- [ ] A marked test explicitly runs the real production `reconcile_loop`; verified by an observable `reconcile_once` signal during lifespan startup.\n- [ ] The worktree passes `make check`, `make test`, Gerrit `LLM-Review +1`, and Gerrit `Verified +1` before submission.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/conftest.py","reason":"Set the suite-wide bounded shutdown drain and register the explicit real-reconciler opt-out marker."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_review_bot.py","reason":"Centralize safe lifespan stubs, migrate duplicated setup, and add RED-first default/escape-hatch regression coverage."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2ae0-abdf-99df-4e69"],["relates_to","478a-15bb-204f-4485"],["relates_to","601f-3a7b-3705-4d31"],["relates_to","db8b-0b2a-f592-4d82"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"26b8f2ce-c5b7-4d13-9d19-55673d3ec0dd","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3b93-a64e-693d-4f5e","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Entering the review-bot app lifespan in a test inherits a 1200s shutdown drain — bound it in tests and make the stubbed path the default","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d5498e30-f121-4b5b-934a-8970241517a0","302208df-a73e-4bfc-a927-1da06f1592af","8a3b24ae-b989-41d6-ad4a-41e369429787","80141cb4-f190-45b5-9109-e994432e2660","2f0d88a4-cb22-48ee-8875-6e51a1be15c9","360c95a9-0d33-4838-89ed-a3201da3e68a","fc8b5c3d-ddf1-4703-907b-bf20267ccb57","478ee765-5206-414c-b721-4e62cc7169b4","32df85af-8f87-4c80-b478-a394f71c9673","9111b187-ce1a-4493-a0af-f8a42fd1d18f","26b8f2ce-c5b7-4d13-9d19-55673d3ec0dd","952909d7-9d5e-47d7-83f9-a2f5d03010c2","5d0cb096-e9ac-48c6-90e8-8b5eb02acad1","60be6b6b-2546-4ada-82ea-e35c453b418b","ee8e17e5-20c9-4a35-a2d8-429f9b900f5e","ae4470a2-7903-444a-88f2-0b6598cd3312","2ec0fd62-7cf2-4fa7-ab2d-d5e7613909f1","20165f08-ea8a-451a-a868-9a2796800872","1a713258-f241-4e93-8676-7557824ec7f2","5cf94f7a-7ef4-4211-af67-ef313d99947c"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786145730614252073,"uuid":"0d204fab-e5d1-47af-b2c9-b03537366df8"}